{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he said. Heavy.</b> Past tense verb, like כִּי זָקֵן יִצְחָק (Genesis 27:1), לוֹ חָפֵץ ד׳ (Judges 13), כַּאֲשֶׁר אָהֵב (Genesis 27:9). The kamatz katan is under the mem of מֵאֵן, which is a root letter, so that the alef after it does not take a dagesh, like חָרֵף נַפְשׁוֹ (Judges 5:18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:23.285049661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}